# The OOM oracle (§1.3/§2.5): the child re-exec dies with the out-of-memory
# panic; keep ONLY the stable prefix of the diagnostic line (request/live
# counts are allocator-state-dependent), so the golden pins that the panic
# fires AND names the 64 KiB fixed heap. A pattern that stops matching makes
# the case fail (the harness rejects a vacuous keep-match).
stdout_keep_match=^out of memory: requested [0-9]+ bytes \(fixed heap 65536 bytes
timeout=600
